Every channel exposes the same contract — that's what lets `NotificationService` treat Email, SMS, and Push identically.

```text
interface Channel:
    method send(user: User, content: RenderedContent): DeliveryResult

class EmailChannel implements Channel:
    private smtpClient: SmtpClient

    method send(user, content): DeliveryResult:
        try:
            smtpClient.sendMail(user.email, content.subject, content.body)
            return DeliveryResult.success()
        catch SmtpTimeoutException as e:
            return DeliveryResult.transientFailure(e.message)

class SMSChannel implements Channel:
    private smsGateway: SmsGatewayClient

    method send(user, content): DeliveryResult:
        try:
            smsGateway.sendText(user.phone, content.body)
            return DeliveryResult.success()
        catch GatewayUnavailableException as e:
            return DeliveryResult.transientFailure(e.message)

class PushChannel implements Channel:
    private pushProvider: PushProviderClient

    method send(user, content): DeliveryResult:
        try:
            pushProvider.push(user.deviceToken, content.title, content.body)
            return DeliveryResult.success()
        catch InvalidTokenException as e:
            return DeliveryResult.permanentFailure(e.message)
```
